{
  "id": "sat-condprob",
  "chapterNumber": "10",
  "title": {
    "en": "Conditional Probability &amp; Two-Way Tables",
    "ar": null
  },
  "chapterTag": {
    "variant": "category",
    "className": "sat-domain-tag",
    "emoji": "📌",
    "categoryPrefix": "Domain:",
    "category": "Problem-Solving &amp; Data Analysis",
    "topics": [
      "Probability and conditional probability",
      "Two-variable data (two-way frequency tables)"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Two-way table questions appear on nearly every Digital SAT. Identify the correct “given” row or column, then divide the joint count by that row/column total.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Probability &amp; Conditional Probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\(P(A)=\\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}}\\). &nbsp;Conditional: \\(P(A\\mid B)=\\dfrac{n(A\\cap B)}{n(B)}\\). &nbsp;Independence: \\(P(A\\mid B)=P(A)\\) — knowing \\(B\\) gives no information about \\(A\\). &nbsp;Complement: \\(P(\\text{not }A)=1-P(A)\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Basic probability",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Conditional \\(P(A\\mid B)\\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{n(A\\cap B)}{n(B)}\\) — restrict to B's row/col",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Independence test",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(P(A\\mid B)=P(A)\\)?",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Complement",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(1-P(A)\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 10.A — Two-way table",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:.87rem\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\"><!-- --></th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Prefers online</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Prefers in-person</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Total</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">Grade 11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">48</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">72</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">120</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">Grade 12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">48</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">80</td></tr><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Total</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">80</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">120</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">200</th></tr></table><p><strong>Q:</strong> Probability of preferring online, given Grade 11?</p>\\[P(\\text{online}\\mid\\text{Gr 11})=\\frac{48}{120}=0.4\\;(40\\%).\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 10.B — Testing independence",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(P(\\text{online})=80/200=0.4\\) and \\(P(\\text{online}\\mid\\text{Gr 11})=0.4\\).</p><p>These are equal, so grade and preference are <strong>independent</strong> in this dataset.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>SAT-style Q1:</strong><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px 0;font-size:.84rem\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\"><span class=\"sr-only\">Row label</span></th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Passed</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Failed</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Total</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">Studied</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">54</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">60</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">Did not study</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px\">40</td></tr><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">Total</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">72</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">28</th><th style=\"border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 12px;background:var(--panel)\">100</th></tr></table>What is \\(P(\\text{passed}\\mid\\text{studied})\\)?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P=54/60=0.9=90\\%\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>SAT-style Q2:</strong> Using the same table, are “passing” and “studying” independent events?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P(\\text{passed})=72/100=0.72\\). \\(P(\\text{passed}\\mid\\text{studied})=0.90\\neq0.72\\). <strong>Not independent</strong> — studying is associated with passing.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
